		{
			"id": "e2J6KJZSuZ9kFT6cF",
			"description": "Chimera",
			"local_notes": "ST/HP 334; Hnd/SR -2/5; HT 11f; Move 2/21; LWt. 38; Load 1.5; SM +5; Occ. 3+12S; DR 250/125 (front 250, side 125, rear 125, top 125, under 125; turret 250/125/125); Locations 2Ct. Control: Driving (Tracked).\n\nTurret multi-laser and hull heavy bolter (the common fit; a heavy flamer can replace the bolter). Six lasgun firing ports along the hull for the squad inside. Amphibious. The turret is an independent turret [t]: losing it leaves the vehicle running.\n\nLore: The Guard's standard armoured transport, built on every forge world from the STC pattern: 38 tonnes, 6.9 m long, up to 70 km/h on a road, crew of three and a full infantry squad of twelve (Imperial Armour Volume One). Front armour AV12, sides and rear AV10.\n\nDesign: HP 2 x 4 x cube root of the curb weight (loaded weight less Load, B463: 73,000 lb) = 334. Front DR 250 (AV12), the rest 125 (AV10). 6.9 m (7.5 yd) gives SM +4, +1 for the box hull: +5. Move 2/21 (70 km/h). Hnd/SR -2/5: a lighter, quicker hull than the Basic Set APC's -3/5.",
