		{
			"id": "e0Ix6GfDSc8vxUqWC",
			"description": "Leman Russ Battle Tank",
			"local_notes": "ST/HP 400; Hnd/SR -3/5; HT 12f; Move 1/11; LWt. 63; Load 0.6; SM +5; Occ. 6S; DR 1350/232 (front 1350, side 340, rear 125, top 125, under 125; turret 1350/340/250); Locations 2CT. Control: Driving (Tracked).\n\nTurret battle cannon (gyro-stabilised: the wargame's Lumbering Behemoth fires it on the move), hull lascannon, heavy bolter sponsons (the sponsons are optional in the field; with them the crew is six). The main turret [T] jams or loses its gun on a major wound and a failed HT roll (B554). The glacis and turret face (DR 1350) stop all but a lucky lascannon hit; take it from the side or rear, or close in with melta.\n\nLore: The backbone of the Imperial Guard's armoured regiments: 63 tonnes, 7.08 m long, 35 km/h on a road, 21 km/h across country, a crew of four plus two sponson gunners (Imperial Armour Volume One). Front AV14, sides AV13, rear AV10; the battle cannon is a large-blast, Strength 8 gun.\n\nDesign: HP 2 x 4 x cube root of the curb weight (124,800 lb) = 400. Front DR 1350 (user direction: the Leman Russ's glacis and turret face are the thickest armour the Guard fields, and only a lucky lascannon shot gets through: 8dx8(5) penetrates 13% of the time, about the wargame's 1 in 6 for Strength 9 against AV14; a meltagun at short range still does 87%, a multi-melta 99%, a krak missile or battle cannon never). Sides 340 (AV13), rear, top and underside 125 (AV10); the turret is as thick at the front and sides and a little better than the hull at the back. 7.08 m (7.7 yd) gives SM +4, +1 for the box: +5. Move 1/11 (35 km/h): as sluggish off the mark as the Basic Set's APC. HT 12: the Leman Russ is famous for keeping going.",
			"tags": [
				"Vehicle",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
