		{
			"id": "ejZ4u1R8aGDfKTsif",
			"description": "Rhino",
			"local_notes": "ST/HP 316; Hnd/SR -2/5; HT 12f; Move 2/21; LWt. 32; Load 1.2; SM +5; Occ. 2+10S; DR 185/155 (front 185, side 185, rear 125, top 125, under 125); Locations 2CX. Control: Driving (Tracked).\n\nA storm bolter on the hatch [X], worked by the commander. Carries ten Space Marines in power armour, or five in Terminator plate is beyond it.\n\nLore: The Astartes' armoured transport, oldest and most common of the STC chassis: 32 tonnes, 6.6 m long, 70 km/h on a road, a crew of two and ten Marines (Imperial Armour Volume Two). AV11 front and sides, AV10 rear.\n\nDesign: HP 2 x 4 x cube root of the curb weight (61,600 lb) = 316. DR 185 front and sides (AV11), 125 rear (AV10). 6.6 m (7.2 yd) gives SM +4, +1 for the box: +5. Crewed by Battle-Brothers: Driving 15.",
