		{
			"id": "eVDKCUVYFGX_WZ0Cy",
			"description": "Land Raider",
			"local_notes": "ST/HP 412; Hnd/SR -3/5; HT 13; Move 1/13; LWt. 70; Load 1.6; SM +6; Occ. 4+10S; DR 1350/1350 (front 1350, side 1350, rear 1350, top 250, under 250); Locations 2C. Control: Driving (Tracked).\n\nTwin-linked lascannon sponsons and a twin-linked heavy bolter in the hull. Linked guns fire together on one roll (the sim fires them as one weapon at twice the rate of fire). Carries ten Space Marines, or five in Terminator plate.\n\nLore: The Adeptus Astartes' heaviest battle tank and assault transport, a relic STC almost no forge world can build: 70 tonnes, 10.3 m long, 40 km/h, armour AV14 all round (Imperial Armour Volume Two). Its machine spirit is said to fight on with the crew dead.\n\nDesign: HP 2 x 4 x cube root of the curb weight (136,800 lb) = 412. DR 1350 all round (user direction: the Leman Russ's glacis on every face, so only a lucky lascannon shot, 13%, gets through from any side; melta up close still does); the roof and belly take 250. 10.3 m (11.3 yd) gives SM +5, +1 for the box: +6. Locations 2C: the sponsons sit in the hull, so no turret. HT 13 for the oldest, best-kept hull the Imperium has.",
