		{
			"id": "eQO6X9GtH9M4UwQNj",
			"description": "Scout Sentinel",
			"local_notes": "ST/HP 96; Hnd/SR +0/3; HT 11f; Move 3/10; LWt. 7; Load 0.2; SM +3; Occ. 1; DR 125/125 (front 125, side 125, rear 125, top 125, under 125); Locations 2LO. Control: Driving (Mecha).\n\nA one-man walker with an open cab [O]: a hit there strikes the pilot, not the hull. The multi-laser is in the cab's chin and fires where the Sentinel faces. Two legs [L]: crippling one drops the walker.\n\nLore: The Guard's reconnaissance walker, about 4.7 m tall and 7 tonnes, a single pilot in an open cab, AV10 all round and open-topped (Imperial Armour Volume One).\n\nDesign: HP 4 x cube root of the curb weight (13,600 lb) = 96 (a light walker, not doubled). DR 125 (AV10) all round. 4.7 m (5.1 yd) tall gives SM +3, an upright figure with no box bonus. Move 3/10: quick off the mark, slow at the top. Its pilot both drives and shoots (the operator's fixed mount, B467: the lower of Gunner and Driving).",
